  "question": {
    "text": "A fair die is tossed repeatedly until a six is obtained. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> denote the number of tosses required and let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>=</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>∣</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mfrac></math> is equal to"
  },
